## Build context exclusions.
##
## Two jobs here. The usual one is keeping the image small. The important one is
## keeping key material and deployment config OUT of the image: several private
## keys and a populated config are tracked on this branch, and a plain `COPY . .`
## bakes them into a layer that is then pushed to a registry. Everything the
## container needs at runtime arrives by bind mount or env instead, see
## deploy/README.md.
##
## Anything added here that the app genuinely needs at runtime must be mounted.

# ── VCS / CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Python build artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# ── Key material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked on this branch (iaca.key, credential_private_key.pem,
# private_nonce_key.pem, ...) and generated locally under pki/. Neither
# belongs in an image. The runtime set is mounted at /etc/eudiw.
*.pem
*.key
*.der
*.crt
*.csr
*.p12
*.jks
pki/
certs/

# ── Deployment config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# config_issuer_backend.yaml is tracked and holds real hostnames/credentials.
# The container reads its config from ISSUER_CONFIG_PATH (a mount) instead.
config_issuer_backend.yaml
config_issuer_backend.*.yaml
app/app_config/config_secrets.py
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/

# ── Host-specific operational scripts ───────────────────────────────────────
# These drive the okeanos VM (hardcoded snf-* hostnames, sudo, certbot paths).
# They are irrelevant inside a container and actively misleading if present.
run-issuer.sh
setup-issuer.sh
resolve-ip.sh
scripts/setup-cert.sh
scripts/setup-venv.sh
scripts/watchdog.py

# ── Local noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
!README.md
tests/
flask_session/
nohup.out
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
